claimed: r-subprocess -- okay-r stage 0 (specs/r.md), the module and
the Rscript engine.

The shape is already built once: okay-py implemented specs/r.md's
model first, and this mirrors it -- REval/RValue/RFrame, a versioned
shim as a resource, the comonadic handler over a clean-env
subprocess, conditions as data, dead-process-throws.

Two things that are R's and not Python's, and both go in the spec:

- NULL and NA are DIFFERENT absences, and NA is TYPED
  (NA_integer_, NA_real_, NA_character_). The py enum has one PyNone;
  RValue needs both, and the spec's own line -- "the R NA story
  stated, not papered over" -- is the test.
- the shim needs jsonlite. Base R has no JSON reader, and writing our
  own parser at the trust boundary is worse than one dependency that
  every R installation used for anything already has. So it is a
  NAMED prerequisite the startup handshake refuses on, not a silent
  import -- a deviation from okay-py's stdlib-only shim, recorded
  with its reason.

Gate: R in a container (r-base plus the Debian r-cran-jsonlite, built
once and cached), reached through a shim at the same absolute path
inside and out -- the sops move. Live and skipped where docker is
absent.

Files: okay-r module + build.sbt, shim.R, tests, specs/r.md, boards.
